# Server conventions

Full context in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.

## Follow `system.js`, not the legacy routes

`routes/system.js` is the target pattern: Knex query builder,
`express-validator` on every endpoint, shared pagination/CSV helpers, and an
audit-log write on every mutation.

`content.js`, `news.js`, `donations.js`, `volunteers.js` and `contact.js` are
legacy raw-SQL routes. When you touch one, move it toward the `system.js`
pattern rather than adding more raw SQL.

## Production is Postgres — SQLite-only SQL will throw

```js
// ❌ BAD — Postgres reads "published" as an identifier, not a string
`WHERE status = "published"`
// ❌ BAD — SQLite-only date functions
`WHERE created_at >= datetime('now', '-30 days')`

// ✅ GOOD
knex('news').where({ status: 'published' })
knex('news').where('created_at', '>=', knex.raw("now() - interval '30 days'"))
```

Single-quote every SQL string literal. Never interpolate user input into SQL —
use bindings or the query builder.

## Routes

- Register literal paths **before** parameterised ones, or `/admin/stats` will
  match `/admin/:id`.
- Validate `:id` params with `param('id').isInt()`.
- Validate enum fields against a whitelist, including `role` on register.
- Protect staff endpoints with `authenticateToken` + `requireAdmin`.

## Schema

Never edit an applied migration; add a new one in `server/migrations/`.

## Donations are pledges

Public submissions save `payment_status: 'pending'` with no `payment_id`. Only
staff mark them received. Never default new donation code to completed.
